      measured:  "9 injected faults ▪ 3 DIVERGENCES, all in pydantic's favour:
                  lowercase id ▪ id too short ▪ line not an int",
      correction: "an earlier note in this cycle recorded the two as EQUAL.
                 The fresh run says otherwise. That note was recall, ¬a
                 measurement, and it was wrong — which is the whole reason the
                 benchmark was re-run instead of cited.",
      what_it_found_in_US: "the register never checked id SHAPE. `owner=ds`
                 had to be hand-corrected today for exactly that reason. Worse
                 on inspection: the EXTRACTOR required an uppercase id, so a
                 marker named wrongly was ¬reported malformed — it VANISHED.
                 A debt that disappears because its name is wrong is the worst
                 outcome for a register whose only job is findability.",
      decision:  "ADOPT THE CHECKS, ¬the dependency. stdlib-only stands (R10).
                 Extractor now permissive, judgement in check(), and the three
                 divergences are closed. Negative-tested: lowercase, too-short
